    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161-a2">

                <pb facs="0276" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg196"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The generals and commandants of the contingents in
                        China to the Dean of the diplomatic corps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the letter from the members of the diplomatic corps, dated June 7, on the
                    return by the provisional government of Tientsin to the Chinese authorities, and
                    in accordance with the demand expressed in paragraph 9 of said letter to inclose
                    you herewith a list of the contracts entered into by the provisional government.
                    I must remark that it is our unanimous <pb facs="0277" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>
                    desire that this list be not communicated to the Chinese authorities before they
                    shall have accepted in principle the maintenance of the validity of these
                    contracts, etc.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Von Rohrecheidt</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">General, Commanding the German Forces in
                                    China</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirchmayr</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Commanding Austrian Forces in
                                China.</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. M. Creaqh</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Major-General, Commanding British Forces in
                                    China.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Lefevre</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">General, Commanding French Troops in
                                    China.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. W. Ameglio</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Colonel, Commanding Italian Forces in
                                    China</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Akiyama</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Colonel, Commanding Japanese Forces in
                                    China.</hi></item>
                            <item>____ ____,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, Commanding Russian
                                    Forces in China</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
